r-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "982e3f94-5d77-5176-9dd4-506289458c9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411088} {:answer/id #uuid "db755250-bc21-584c-bdb8-21fc812b84ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411097}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411088} :answer-field/id #uuid "46669123-e51d-59ed-bd9d-af7b5c1b87de" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d8ab9c9-3b6e-506c-b947-40d6834bbb92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "≡" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411089} {:answer/id #uuid "e635ecab-3c5c-52ff-926d-41857ac215dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "≢" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411099}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411099} :answer-field/id #uuid "581c9f72-306d-54b6-94af-e6d8a7a94201" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "370f4c3f-99c1-5afb-8d47-cb9a74d1c85e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411072} {:answer/id #uuid "791854e7-a7e6-524b-b5e9-1dc27fcbd843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411083}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411072} :answer-field/id #uuid "d440bf3f-9095-5263-9a45-107c23d37fbf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411114}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "31ca1a18-e271-54de-8d6a-f0aa14857b82" :question/math-academy-id "q-182517" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\n \n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B){{field-4}}A\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∨¬(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{F}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{F}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ is logically equivalent to $A,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nWe see that the columns for $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ and $A$ are different. They differ in the second and third rows. Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)≢A.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0ff445d2-7e9e-5a92-baf5-6ddc40e4b354"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420442 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ff3ba28-38e8-51bc-a126-2eff2903bff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472574} {:answer/id #uuid "2d8239a8-397c-5bf4-8f09-ac6412a0e0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472575}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472575} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d4328ce-d94c-50ad-9bc6-66e180d0c379" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de4aeae3-2eea-55f8-9d3b-f6f28669d75a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472576} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb9487c-635d-5949-9980-a665c9ff96ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472577}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472577} :answer-field/id #uuid "21b67704-7d9c-5f26-8cd4-1364e0247ba7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473683} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "428e1b82-e6da-5eab-9b6a-0c2af131b494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472578} {:answer/id #uuid "d54291b6-7ef2-55e0-96fb-76e1195bcd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472579}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472578} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa69a530-25df-51d2-8915-d0fef8fbe9e6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b8076c0f-174e-5d1d-bedf-553b0bcc1d94" :question/math-academy-id "q-127969" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nI. $¬Q∧(P∨Q)$\n\nII. $P∧¬Q$\n\nIII. $¬P∧¬Q$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q∧(P∨Q)\\,$ | $\\,P∧¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∧¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬Q∧(P∨Q)$ and $P∧¬Q$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "18fbff04-a217-5de2-878b-afa2ebaa94f8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420443}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420443 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157632 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eed8fd4-6bcd-5077-a365-1911e8e388c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411076} {:answer/id #uuid "7d501d86-5ee8-5bf1-abca-e025a206e6b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411085}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411076} :answer-field/id #uuid "149af20b-492b-566d-9400-bf00e13bfd30" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fd808a4-c11b-550d-9ea2-7d4cd9978ac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411069} {:answer/id #uuid "d07a632f-a215-52fb-8b7e-a1ce0e990b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411096}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411096} :answer-field/id #uuid "427549ac-c517-584c-833b-e3067bc01788" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d4b249d-38f3-5cbc-8a3f-4a5d46ce6a98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "≢" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411079} {:answer/id #uuid "c62534a0-136c-52bb-a53c-b21ec75b5158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "≡" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411092}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411092} :answer-field/id #uuid "70cb2a41-cfff-576e-90ca-abdb122477cf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23622841-3128-577e-a7e0-95dbaa45288a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411070} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d600ce-3590-58fd-99ec-92daf40af5b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411100}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411070} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce54b23b-99a2-54a1-b4c2-0560201db0dd" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "10f78fd8-b244-51f6-bc65-b2ef2428fc6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-182344" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧B)\\,$ | $\\,¬A∨¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B){{field-4}}¬A∨¬B\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬A∨¬B & ≡¬\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬A∨¬B & ≡¬\\text{T}∨¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{F}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(A∧B) & ≡¬(\\text{F}∧\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧B)\\,$ | $\\,¬A∨¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $¬(A∧B)$ is logically equivalent to $¬A∨¬B,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{T},\\text{T}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)≡¬A∨¬B.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "762f22a6-54a9-512b-a9ec-3247d07fe0b7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420444}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420444 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42f09717-d982-51ef-bc12-71e8f554d51e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411077} {:answer/id #uuid "afb3b338-228a-5862-9d02-389bb7109931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411091}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411077} :answer-field/id #uuid "335db4d0-e78a-5086-8228-fb291ff6c553" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0150989f-9b6c-5f03-9a0b-cccc272d9946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1