| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add columns for $¬A$ and $¬B:$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for the part of the expression that's in parentheses, $¬A∧¬B:$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $B∨(¬A∧¬B):$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧¬B\\,$ | $\\,B∨(¬A∧¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |"} :step/id #uuid "bb2e7002-cb35-5307-b21f-a9167f224eb6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420441}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420445 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d27ca29e-af01-5502-b7f1-b8e28f314afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460317} {:answer/id #uuid "2535d370-b9e9-50c4-83d0-ab4059bc1fc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460318}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460318} :answer-field/id #uuid "41760cd3-9dd5-5e91-bb72-ce0b2c74c79b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177114ef-01a6-5ed0-a402-4831e768f76a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460319} {:answer/id #uuid "5d7a4af3-80d4-5e47-80e6-2bd3164a15de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460320}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460320} :answer-field/id #uuid "8389f0b7-18d7-5be7-85f0-8f79a6ad9188" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e92d461f-41c7-5578-b208-7d2c6c3729bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460321} {:answer/id #uuid "4250ef8d-0db6-535f-a90f-5adee0079036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460322}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460322} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd3e95a-2be7-576c-97fd-864d4440ee21" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "39f394a7-df4a-5b3c-93b6-e97b645cd2dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-81351" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nI. $X∧¬Y$\n\nII. $¬(Y∨¬X)$\n\nIII. $¬Y∧(X∨X)$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,X∧¬Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(Y∨¬X)\\,$ | $\\,¬Y∧(X∨X)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nWe see that all three statements have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} :step/id #uuid "d8c45790-8fd7-51e2-a9d0-768c5d684a5d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420442}}] :activity/title "Logical Equivalence" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420440}]}
